# WIN-PUBLIC-SITE — Phase 0 follow-up, sub-agent M

File: openOODA/audit/win_public_site.oot
Date: 2026-08-19. Lane: read-only public-site audit. Sub-agent: M.
Scope: door, 7 guide pages, registry, install script, 4 Windows audit files.
Pin checked: v0.205.0-beta.

## 0. Headline

The public site is honest. Every Windows, Mac, or Linux ARM mention is a disclaimer, not a product claim. No page promises a Windows compiler, a Windows installer, `ooda install` on Windows, or a stock-store-as-first-machine. The single edge: the door (`index.html`) shows the install command with no platform caveat next to it. The caveat lives one link away on the `Start` page. The audit below records the trade and proposes a one-line fix.

## 1. Door (`openOODA.github.io/index.html`)

| # | Claim text | Line | Verdict | Reason |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 1 | `openOODA` (title, meta) | 6,7,9,10 | honest | brand only, no platform |
| 2 | `v0.205.0-beta` | 193 | honest | matches audit pin |
| 3 | `curl -fsSL https://openooda.org/install | bash` | 209, 287 | under-claim (see §6) | honest install command, but no platform line on the door itself; the `Start` page is one link away |
| 4 | `On Linux, &SysCap can apply a Landlock jail and POSIX setrlimit.` | 218 | honest | explicit "On Linux" gate; matches the chs_rt audit finding that Landlock is Linux-only and the Windows shim uses Job Objects |
| 5 | `~/.local/bin/ooda` / `~/.local/bin/oodac` / `~/.local/share/ooda/std/` / `~/.local/share/ooda/runtime/` / `~/.local/share/ooda/share/fixtures/hello.oo` / `~/.config/ooda/env` | 248-253 | honest as Linux fact, under-claim for cross-platform | XDG paths. Correct on Linux. Phase 4 (`win_compiler_plan.oot:100-110`) will move these to `%LOCALAPPDATA%\openooda\bin\ooda.exe`. The door does not say "only Linux," so a Windows user could be misled. See §6. |
| 6 | `ooda run typechecks, emits C, calls host gcc, and runs the binary.` | 256 | honest | "host gcc" is platform-bound. Acceptable as the everyday path. The audit at `win_c_emit_compat.oot:154` says chs_rt blocks the first Windows .exe link today, so this matches reality. |
| 7 | mail-list form posts to `https://collect.openooda.org/v1/emails` | 261, 329 | honest | no platform claim; identical across OS |

Dead links on the door: none. All anchors point to `#Guide.oot` and `https://registry.openooda.org/`, both present.

